  "result": "`Parameter.consume_value` (`core.py:2481`) resolves a value in this order of precedence, and each step runs only if the value is still `UNSET`:\n\n1. **Command line.** It reads `opts.get(self.name, UNSET)`, which holds whatever the parser produced. If a value is found, the source is `ParameterSource.COMMANDLINE`.\n2. **Environment variable.** It calls `self.value_from_envvar(ctx)`. If the result is not `None`, it uses that value and sets the source to `ENVIRONMENT`.\n3. **default_map.** It calls `ctx.lookup_default(self.name)`. The value is taken if it is not `None`, or if the key exists in the map (`_default_map_has`), so an explicit `None` still counts. The source is `DEFAULT_MAP`. If the value is a string and `nargs != 1`, it is split with `type.split_envvar_value`, as environment values are.\n4. **Parameter default.** It calls `self.get_default(ctx)`. If that is not `UNSET`, the value is used and the source is `DEFAULT`.\n\nThe source starts as `DEFAULT` whenever the parser supplied nothing. If every step comes up empty, the value stays `UNSET` and the source stays `DEFAULT`.\n\nThe method returns a `(value, source)` tuple. The caller records the source on the context.\n\n`Option.consume_value` (`core.py:3589`) wraps the base method. It can override the source to `PROMPT` when a flag needs a value and a prompt is set, or to `COMMANDLINE` when a flag is activated without a value.\n\nI didn't modify any files.",
